{"name": "r1102-15", "sha256": "9683492beb2151fe161e6d02ce2d2a7c18de11c89cd8f9f0050857c5a9b89f11", "words": 187, "headline": "AI Detected", "prediction_short": "Mixed", "fraction_ai": 0.1417626589536667, "fraction_ai_assisted": 5.522517247904104e-42, "fraction_human": 0.8582373261451721, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/1050793a-1f08-47d0-aac9-098afd0e5408", "utc": "2026-11-02T17:03:41Z", "windows": [["Human Written", "High", 112, 0, 580, "The inner child, the guards, and the inner adult’s three jobs\nYour inner child won’t trust you right away. It’s not going to be enough for you to meditate, say three nice sentences to the inner child and expect to have its trust. What’s going to help your inner child to trust you is you, the person you are right now, becoming reliable.\nHere I’m going to talk about what you develop in yourself as you reparent your inner child. I’m going to talk about it in terms of three jobs: your loving Nurturer, your safe Adult Protector (hereafter just the Protector) and your wise Guide."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 27, 580, 715, " That’s one grown-up doing three jobs, not three more people moving in to help with the rent, and each job keeps the others in balance."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 9, 715, 763, " It’s you that needs to develop these qualities."], ["Human Written", "High", 37, 763, 978, "\nAlso, your inner child’s worth is not dependent on these qualities… It has its own worth, and its own qualities, like playing, being tender, not taking life too seriously, being creative and wondering at the world."], ["Human Written", "Low", 12, 978, 1046, " Those belong in your relationship with it too, not just the wounds."]]}
{"name": "r1102-18", "sha256": "c5ef120acbed4903c051c7afaca154599af8901f574a7d05a461531792fad55e", "words": 345, "headline": "Human Written", "prediction_short": "Human", "fraction_ai": 5.3865944943903476e-21, "fraction_ai_assisted": 7.290714980175318e-33, "fraction_human": 1.0, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/c6b36d22-219d-4ae0-a41a-058aa230d561", "utc": "2026-11-02T17:03:45Z", "windows": [["Human Written", "High", 356, 0, 1828, "Love doesn’t have to wait for trust\nWhat if your little one doesn't believe you love them? It is possible to love them even if they don't believe you love them. Their trust can question your promises, remember when you failed to protect them, and take its time, and you can keep loving them while it does.\nYou could say something like, \"Okay. I believe that you don't believe me. I still love you. You don't have to love me back. Tell me what feels unsafe.\" Try not to turn \"I still love you\" into a line you say on cue, though, because then it can brush the anger off, and what it's really saying is \"so stop being angry.\"\nThen respond to the complaints that are sure to come. You don't have to accept every conclusion they reach about you, but do listen for the concrete complaint without fighting the yelling and swearing around it, because even if they are coming from a place that is not completely \"right,\" there will likely be something true in what they are saying. If it's something serious, answer it seriously. Do what you can to show your love for them. This might include some or all of the following: Learning to listen to them when they are angry without hitting back. Owning what was not okay. Working on changing yourself so that you are less likely to turn on them. Finding other ways to make up to them for what you did. Finding other ways to show your love for them (this might include taking care of them, such as by buying and cooking food for them, setting limits for them, taking them to the doctor when they need it, and doing what you said you would do). Just not hitting back is enough to start being the adult, even if it isn't enough yet for them to trust you. Even that takes some warmth, and if you don't have any yet, borrow some from someone who's been good to you, or from an adult you imagine."]]}
{"name": "r1102-20", "sha256": "f25faaa75b127d2455a2bbd617e506c31a55519f1661698b6478085f73ca3d00", "words": 246, "headline": "Human Written", "prediction_short": "Human", "fraction_ai": 5.806378815254032e-12, "fraction_ai_assisted": 2.301445453827926e-27, "fraction_human": 1.0, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/2a24658b-12cb-4fe3-99d5-7f491077a470", "utc": "2026-11-02T17:03:52Z", "windows": [["Human Written", "High", 75, 0, 409, "Working with your inner child\nThe two-hand practice\nThere is a simple and easy body technique to connect with your inner child. Just place one hand in the center of your chest, which physically connects you to your love, and then place your other hand just below that, on your solar plexus, where your inner child can be.\nImagine a divine Love from above, with the inner child below, in the solar plexus area."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 5, 409, 437, " The inner adult is present."], ["Human Written", "High", 78, 437, 804, " You can also use the hand on the solar plexus to massage that area.\nBegin to send love from your heart down to your inner child and just notice what comes up for you. If some comes back up, let it, and send it on down again, so it goes around like a loop. That part's a gift from them, and they don't owe it to you, so if nothing comes back, just keep sending yours."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 9, 804, 852, " If you feel resistance, just meet it with love."], ["Human Written", "High", 13, 852, 916, " If you feel or see something, just meet that with love as well."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 29, 916, 1057, " If you can't find any warmth today, just leave your hands where they are and notice what's there. Don't pretend to feel something you don't."], ["Human Written", "High", 17, 1057, 1149, " Let it go back and forth between your heart and your inner child, like a real conversation."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 7, 1149, 1199, "\nKeep breathing gently through the whole practice."], ["Human Written", "High", 20, 1199, 1298, " It works as an induction too: the Sober induction below has it as one of the anchors you can pick."]]}
{"name": "r1102-23", "sha256": "94091de8df404efc9ee26c84f970315356a9522a4c33f114a26b5f30da868478", "words": 470, "headline": "Human Written", "prediction_short": "Human", "fraction_ai": 6.20556264152583e-08, "fraction_ai_assisted": 2.5018663403084927e-33, "fraction_human": 0.9999999403953552, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/ea5ab290-9965-40a1-83c3-bae3634cf0d3", "utc": "2026-11-02T17:03:59Z", "windows": [["Human Written", "High", 127, 0, 699, "Working with your guards\nUse parts language here too, if it helps. Often, we see a sensation or a distraction or an objection as something that needs to be explored, when in fact it might just be hunger, or reasonable skepticism about something, or a sentence that doesn’t fit. Still, notice it, and then look at what might be going on.\nIf you're not careful, you might find yourself expecting that when you go within to meet your inner child, you'll find your inner child.\nInstead, you might feel numb, cynical, angry, suddenly hungry, like you need to look at your phone, sexually aroused, like you need to make plans, sleepy, dissociated, or you might even think that what you're doing is stupid."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 4, 699, 723, " Those are not failures."], ["Human Written", "High", 32, 723, 908, " Often what you're experiencing is a very charming guard. It's what protects you when your consciously installed parental Protector isn't functioning, the same as when you were a child."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 9, 908, 948, " It might not be a guard at all, though."], ["Human Written", "High", 15, 948, 1017, " Maybe it's your inner child, mad that you took so long to come back."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 17, 1017, 1109, " Maybe it's your inherited parent script, or something from earlier today, or a bit of each."], ["Human Written", "Low", 21, 1109, 1205, " So before you decide where it's coming from, ask it what it's trying to stop, or what it wants."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 16, 1205, 1284, "\nTalk to the guard the way your Nurturer talks to your inner child: “I see you."], ["Human Written", "Low", 10, 1284, 1324, " I'm not going to force my way past you."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 25, 1324, 1448, " What's going on?” Then wait and listen patiently. If nothing comes back, that's okay, you don't need to push for an answer."], ["Human Written", "High", 213, 1448, 2534, " Later on, you can ask it, “What are you afraid would happen if you stopped protecting me by…?”\nIf necessary, take time and listen. (Perhaps they are afraid that you will lie to yourself again or pretend again or that it will be too painful or you will spiritually bypass again or you will forgive someone who shouldn’t be forgiven yet or you will see what you want to see or that you will leave them hanging after the session or…)\nNow talk to the guard. Tell them that it makes sense that they want to protect you and that they don’t have to stop protecting you, but that you want to know what could make them trust you 1% more that you can protect yourself. If it says no, I’d listen, and if it says no to going deeper in this work or to an altered state, I’d stop there and not push past that no, even when it sounds like a prediction.\nMost of the time, the guard wants you to do certain things: set boundaries, do whatever you are supposed to do, eat, not text someone, keep a promise, go to sleep, talk to the therapist, admit that you owe someone money, write something down, etc."]]}
{"name": "r1102-27", "sha256": "d29a03f64f4be927c420e9f739bd14b25de70e69c2deb1a01e4b4f15d5e2be93", "words": 428, "headline": "Mostly Human Written", "prediction_short": "Human", "fraction_ai": 0.0583735890686512, "fraction_ai_assisted": 1.3890899966307505e-21, "fraction_human": 0.9416264295578003, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/03338373-12c4-41ab-bbda-694159cd0d2e", "utc": "2026-11-02T17:04:06Z", "windows": [["Human Written", "Low", 48, 0, 249, "Don’t rush the repair\nWhen your inner child does show up, spend some quality time with them before taking off the kid gloves, so to speak, and jumping into the healing work.\nThey might like to hear something like, “Little one, I’m here with you now."], ["Human Written", "Low", 9, 249, 293, " You don’t have to work to explain anything."], ["Human Written", "Low", 15, 293, 360, " I'm not asking you to impress me with how fast you can get better."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 13, 360, 426, " Can I help you feel less alone?”\nWhat does your inner child need?"], ["Human Written", "High", 38, 426, 646, " It can be anything: warmth, to play, to be protected, to mourn, to be angry, food, rest, boundaries, better relationships, to stop fantasizing, to stop working their butt off, that you keep a promise to them today, etc."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 1, 646, 651, " etc."], ["Human Written", "High", 37, 651, 840, "\nWhen a younger you, a guard, a feeling or a signal comes up in your body, take it slowly:\nA. Prepare yourself to tend to them with some privacy, but still able to access support if needed."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 52, 840, 1132, " Check how much grown-up you is really in the room first. Can you take a moment before you react? When you decide something, do you follow through? If you answered \"No,\" because right now you’re mostly still stuck identifying as the frightened little boo, hold off on the deeper conversation."], ["Human Written", "High", 14, 1132, 1199, " Do what makes you feel adult before you try to talk to little you."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 1, 1199, 1202, "\nB."], ["Human Written", "High", 12, 1202, 1262, " Look at what's there before judging or deciding what it is."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 1, 1262, 1265, "\nC."], ["Human Written", "High", 37, 1265, 1465, " Ask them what you can do or if you can move closer to them. Even if you feel like you already know what they need, ask if they'd prefer warmth, space, verbal reassurance, silence, distance, whatever."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 1, 1465, 1468, "\nD."], ["Human Written", "High", 16, 1468, 1547, " Give them what you can: pick a need and do the smallest thing that would help."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 11, 1547, 1590, " Don't feel like you have to fix it all.\nE."], ["Human Written", "High", 21, 1590, 1690, " Give yourself some time to let what you did sink in- it may take some time, it may take sleep, etc."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 1, 1690, 1693, "\nF."], ["Human Written", "High", 24, 1693, 1828, " Reconnect with them- don't expect them to merge, go away, forgive you, become happy, etc. Just reconnect with them if they're willing."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 1, 1828, 1831, "\nG."], ["Human Written", "High", 89, 1831, 2294, " Stop and rest before the caring turns into another performance, and reconnect with them later to see what was helpful.\nRemember the goal isn't to make yourself good as new but to make yourself good as you- more supported and connected to yourself. If you don't like the idea of part work or it makes you feel more divided, you can work with a signal or a feeling instead of a part, or with an imaginary younger you that you feel embodies the issue you're having."]]}
{"name": "r1102-37", "sha256": "760bbd062c0e02d8df4b017d8749a800f4c09fca6a81e5cee466dc57c5dbaf76", "words": 541, "headline": "Human Written", "prediction_short": "Human", "fraction_ai": 4.1113132727898724e-15, "fraction_ai_assisted": 1.3460110121616078e-28, "fraction_human": 1.0, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/df0f0002-33f7-4e0e-8ee2-443ab40e7775", "utc": "2026-11-02T17:04:11Z", "windows": [["Human Written", "High", 205, 0, 1104, "Before you begin\nRead through the induction, and the Come all the way back section, when you're awake.\nGet clear on what it is you want to do during the induction. What are you leaving alone today? How long do you want to spend on this? (You don't have to do this on a problem. You can do it on something you want to experience more of: love, play, confidence, creativity, communion, whatever.) Make sure you're leaving some time at the end to come back, and reflect on what you experienced.\nPut yourself in a place where you can safely do this, which is not: driving a big machine, swimming with the fishies, or otherwise needing to be alert and functionally responsible for yourself or others. If you are intoxicated and more confused than usual, or for whatever reason not able to keep yourself safe, then get some immediate support instead of doing exploratory hypnosis. (The part below called \"When you're already trancey\" can be used to help orient you if you're already open, but don't use it to make yourself deeper if you're not stable.)\nDeciding to do it: how will you coax yourself to do this?"], ["Human Written", "Medium", 3, 1104, 1122, " Make it spacious?"], ["Human Written", "High", 14, 1122, 1189, " Make it warm and held? Make it firmer, so you stay with a feeling?"], ["Human Written", "Medium", 2, 1189, 1205, " Something else?"], ["Human Written", "High", 330, 1205, 2833, " Preview what you are going to do: will you close your eyes? Will you come out and go back in again? What will you do at the end? If you are going to use a recording, read the script beforehand if you can. Know that you can say \"stop\" at any time and the induction will end. If you want to change something, say \"less\" if you want it to ask less of you, or say \"quiet\" and the talking will stop. You can also just open your eyes and stop, and then come all the way back anyway. You don't need to ask any parts for permission to stop, even if a part tells you that you do.\nIf you are new to this or haven't done it for a while, work on the coming in and coming out part first. Don't bring in the hard stuff till later. You don't have to watch yourself all the time, but for the first few times, make sure you can change state. Let yourself make it easier and easier to do this and notice that it takes less and less of you to do it. A no will stay a no. The narrator can't add stuff just because you don't say anything.\nLet your response guide you as to what to do next regardless of what the script is expecting. Utilize: use what you have (a thought, sound, movement, or objection) to go to the next place, whatever it is. Learn how to notice what is there. If nothing changes, notice that too. As my dad always said, \"Be prepared to take what you get. The best might come afterwards!\" For more on language you can use, see Appendix B, or keep reading below for information on using the tools after induction in Let the next response guide you. Either way, keep the instructions about how to stay safe and how to get out plain."]]}
{"name": "r1102-39", "sha256": "0e61db748fdab93668668e5b4fd71415dbab85968cc47acb9e4b0970bb4cfeab", "words": 191, "headline": "Human Written", "prediction_short": "Human", "fraction_ai": 1.8653867784202555e-14, "fraction_ai_assisted": 1.568085954109915e-32, "fraction_human": 1.0, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/95276a1f-769a-4d22-a7ec-152267521f07", "utc": "2026-11-02T17:04:15Z", "windows": [["Human Written", "High", 56, 0, 345, "When you’re already trancey\nThis is for when something has already opened you up before you start: loveyhuasca, meditation, lucid dreaming, going through grief, listening to beautiful music, prayer, erotic energy, exhaustion, seeing something you love, etc.\nKnow that you're already open, you just need to aim and stabilize it, and keep it kind."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 23, 345, 468, "\nOrient yourself by looking around. Where are you? What's the date or day? How does your body feel? Where are you grounded?"], ["Human Written", "High", 33, 468, 650, " Can you feel your feet/hands/spine/etc? Make some contact with yourself, eg press your thumbs against the tips of your index fingers gently but firmly so that you can feel friction."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 3, 650, 665, " Focus on that."], ["Human Written", "High", 62, 665, 983, "\nSay something like, \"I ask to experience only the therapy that I can integrate. Patience pays, so if there's too much, let it simmer. May my body stay safe, and may my little one know there's an adult here to carry the heavy stuff.\"\nOnce you’ve got your bearings, make your first wish.\n\"Please show me the next truth."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 5, 983, 1011, " The next symbol or feeling."], ["Human Written", "High", 19, 1011, 1101, " The question or action that's useful for me at this time, and no more than I can handle.\""]]}
{"name": "r1102-40", "sha256": "bc063a1ba5d0fd9df23cfad870f7d7f74703f5306782308226f078bcdd69efa6", "words": 316, "headline": "AI Detected", "prediction_short": "Mixed", "fraction_ai": 0.503777027130127, "fraction_ai_assisted": 3.3524328513473885e-29, "fraction_human": 0.49622297286987305, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/93ac0152-0715-4cde-b8ff-d6544781099d", "utc": "2026-11-02T17:04:19Z", "windows": [["Human Written", "Medium", 37, 0, 183, "Stay awake when your mind likes to escape\nIf your mind keeps drifting off, sit up and open your eyes. Then feel your feet on the floor, and just let your breathing go at its own pace."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 16, 183, 274, " Tell yourself, \"I'm not going anywhere. I'm happily arriving more fully here each moment.\""], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 32, 274, 440, "\nPick something in the room to look at, and feel your spine at the same time (focusing on two things makes it harder for the mind to use multitasking mode to wander)."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 10, 440, 497, " Then ask yourself what the daydreaming is doing for you."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 5, 497, 526, " Is it bringing you guidance?"], ["Human Written", "Low", 16, 526, 607, " Does it help you work through a feeling, or are you using it to avoid something?"], ["Human Written", "Low", 23, 607, 730, "\nAsk for any diffuse benefits to become more practically focused: \"If this is guidance, show me what I need to do about it."], ["Human Written", "High", 48, 730, 1005, " If I'm avoiding something, bring me gently back to the present and show me what it is.\"\nMake the hypnosis more alert\nAside from focusing on things in your direct experience, you can also suggest yourself into greater alertness (it's still relaxed-alert, not paranoid-alert)."], ["Human Written", "Low", 34, 1005, 1190, " Keep your eyes open. Use a small hand movement each time you make the auto-suggestion that you're gaining increasing clarity. Then stop the hand movement and see where your mind is at."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 12, 1190, 1252, " That hand movement is the mental escape into the body's flow."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 42, 1252, 1484, " Say something like,\n“Starting with your eyes open, press your thumb to your forefinger, gently, and let go. As you do, you begin to bring yourself into a place of clearer awareness… Press and let go again, and you’re clearer still."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 10, 1484, 1541, " And once more, into the clearest state of awareness yet."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 3, 1541, 1560, " Now stop pressing."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 29, 1560, 1713, " In the first second after you stop, notice if there’s any echo of the pressing in your fingers, in your breathing, in your attention, or nowhere at all."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 10, 1713, 1769, " Just notice, sit up straight and work from this level.”"]]}
{"name": "r1102-41", "sha256": "ef6fda9141a61c4a02a04dc11d8a290e6170682e0686e63d832459be8ceec2c2", "words": 200, "headline": "Human Written", "prediction_short": "Human", "fraction_ai": 1.7531890423811346e-18, "fraction_ai_assisted": 5.823757251147002e-25, "fraction_human": 1.0, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/2d4a21bf-a0aa-4166-a095-ee4ef45c0ee3", "utc": "2026-11-02T17:04:29Z", "windows": [["Human Written", "High", 202, 0, 1086, "Sleep induction\nSleep induction is different than inner work, where you need to come back up to write things down and act on them.\nYou can tell your analytical mind to stand down, any revelations can wait.\nCheck out Nimja’s sleep playlist to go to sleep listening to hypnosis.\nOptional fractionation: practice coming back\nFractionation means coming partway back toward normal awareness, then deciding whether to go back into the trance. It gives the trance a revolving door, so you can check how the session is going from a few different depths instead of \"flying blind.\" Going in and out a few times also makes going in and coming out easier and quicker, until it feels natural. At some point in a session, you can do it on purpose, like this:\n“Okay, open your eyes and come back up. Feel the room around you. You can decide if you want to stop the work at this point or continue. If you want to continue, soften your eyes or close them, and notice the change that comes over you when you do. If you want to stop, that’s okay too. Either way is okay, and you can stop at either place.”"]]}
{"name": "r1102-51", "sha256": "9bbad1024e89830795f0acad9427ac834e492f90c1bd14206fa8a9bbea597a28", "words": 346, "headline": "Human Written", "prediction_short": "Human", "fraction_ai": 3.2194302883204815e-17, "fraction_ai_assisted": 3.185598255464613e-37, "fraction_human": 1.0, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/9dcc5db7-cf60-43a1-a859-e09eea95ed67", "utc": "2026-11-02T17:04:33Z", "windows": [["Human Written", "High", 86, 0, 460, "Finish without forcing a revelation\nDon’t feel that you have to end the session with a great revelation (those are often flaky, not standing the test of time). When you have done as much as you want to do, ask yourself what would help you leave things where they are for now. This might include thanking parts for their help, or making sure that you do something in real life (put a boundary in place, get some rest, repair a relationship, keep a promise etc)."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 25, 460, 586, " You can tell your little one, \"That’s enough for today, choochoo. Aren't you excited to get back to the life we're building?\""], ["Human Written", "High", 244, 586, 1881, "\nWhen you have finished, even if you stopped part way through, use the ‘Come all the way back’ procedure to bring yourself back. When you are back, it is a good idea to write a few lines in a notebook about what you have done. Just jot down the essentials (what was there before you started, what you have done to change things, what happened, what you are unsure about, any phrases that were said, any body signals, any information that the inner child said that it needed, anything that a guard wanted you to know, any boundaries that you put in place, any repairs that you did, anything you learned about what not to force etc). You don’t have to list every part of you that might have been involved, only what you actually noticed.\nThroughout the exercise\nAllow your analytical part to make comments and/or tell you that it doesn’t like what you are doing. Just tell it that you will check things out, and make any commitments etc, when you are back. If it says no to going deeper, or tells you to stop doing the exercise, I’d stop there. You can stop whenever you want to. Remember that the images you see can be meaningful without being memories of things that actually happened. And just because you see an image, or feel a body release, doesn’t mean you are right about what is going on."]]}
{"name": "r1102-69", "sha256": "f63b05836ad19de568115f5303fb773d82cdff98261ce56e64b5a0652fc12c6f", "words": 1211, "headline": "Human Written", "prediction_short": "Human", "fraction_ai": 1.1351621651556343e-06, "fraction_ai_assisted": 2.162951482499257e-32, "fraction_human": 0.9999988675117493, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/b6b3ac4c-810e-4d4f-a2db-15d7bd4125fe", "utc": "2026-11-02T17:04:40Z", "windows": [["Human Written", "High", 413, 0, 2151, "The Milton Model, minus the covert sales seminar\nWe are going to use a model that’s called the Milton model. It’s all to do with sentence architecture. When we tell ourselves to ‘be better’, ‘relax now’, ‘stop feeling anxious’ or ‘trust me’, it doesn’t work, does it?\nWhat we need to do is use indirect language to go around the part that wants to argue with us, so that we can actually get to where we want to get to.\nSo let’s start with something we know to be true, let’s take the pressure off, presume that we can only do a tiny bit and let’s invite one thing:\n‘As my body begins to notice the sensation of the bed underneath it, it may be possible for it to begin to realize that it is not alone in carrying the burden of the day.’\nWe paced it; we opened up awareness; we validated the reason for the reaction; we presumed we could do it; we used a bridge word to make it easier and we invited one thing. We can then test this out with the body to see if it was possible.\nPattern 1: Pacing and leading — truth before suggestion\nSo how might we pace and lead in a way that works with anxiety?\nIt might go something like this: ‘It is completely true that the sensation of ________ (or the emotion of _____) is coming up for me. It makes complete sense that my system is trying to react and respond to that by wanting to do or think ________. While that is completely true, there is another thing that is equally true, which is that my adult self is here, breathing in the room right now, and wanting to listen to what comes up for me next.’\nTruth, Invite, Truth, Invite etc. is all you need to do.\nPattern 2: Awareness verbs\nOpen up awareness by using awareness verbs e.g. notice, realize, recognize, sense, feel, wonder, imagine, picture, listen to, allow, discover, remember, consider etc.\nExample: ‘Notice how the answer comes to you… maybe as an image, or a word… maybe as a pressure, or some warmth… or a silence, or a sense of what to do next.’\nPattern 3: Presuppositions\nA presupposition hides an assumption inside a sentence, and whoever hears it usually just goes along with it. That’s a lot of power, so only use it to assume good things."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 8, 2151, 2193, " It should give you more agency, not less."], ["Human Written", "High", 136, 2193, 2918, " It should make you more safe (not just feeling more safe when you're not). It should help you feel the love that's there (even if it's only available beyond the conditions). We don't use this to assume obedience, the way a less ethical hypnotist does when they say something like, ‘As you go deeper, it gets easier and easier to just do what I say.’\nI'd switch that up to the safe version: ‘As you go deeper, it gets easier to commune with any part that needs your understanding before it can change.’\nPattern 4: Gentle cause-effect bridges\nBridge words, like ‘as’, ‘whilst’, ‘because’, ‘when’, ‘after’, ‘before’ and ‘which means’, link one event to the next, so the first can seem to come with the second, or even cause it."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 8, 2918, 2956, " That doesn't mean it does, of course."], ["Human Written", "High", 138, 2956, 3736, " This is another kind of more subtle presupposition technique.\nWe can use this technique to support communion and agency: “As I breathe, my adult self can allow itself to become present enough to hear a bit of what my wounded inner child needs.”\nPattern 5: Embedded invitations\nAn embedded invitation tucks a small direction inside a bigger sentence, like when you put a pill inside a little food to swallow it easier. In communion hypnosis, we choose not to use embeds like this to hide commands, but rather to soften them into nudges. Nudges give more agency, and they keep the conversation flowing without a need for a strong decision. For example, rather than, \"As I sit here, I will become aware...\" we can say, \"As I sit here, I may begin to allow myself to become aware...\""], ["Human Written", "Medium", 32, 3736, 3887, "\nWith your inner child, it could be: \"My little one doesn't have to trust me all at once. I invite them to just notice that right now, I'm still here.\""], ["Human Written", "High", 321, 3887, 5690, "\nInvitational language can also feel super fake though, especially when it's overused. Fakeness doesn't feel so safe. And if it's just chunking the manipulation into easier bite-sized portions without reducing the overall size of the demand, it could be less ethical, not more.\nPattern 6: Ethical double binds\nThis is also an actual parenting technique. Children love choices, even when they're both designed for the same pre-decided outcome. Our subconscious still works like that, too. A manipulative double bind is the name for that, although hypnotists don't call it manipulative, that's my framing. Nimja demonstrates this a lot in his hypnosis: \"Do you want to go deeper now, or in a moment?\" Clearly, that sends you deeper regardless what you \"choose.\"\nAn ethical double bind also gives you two choices, but both of them are designed to be genuinely safe, and they also give a bit of actual agency, even if both choices serve the same end. Example:\n\"Welcome to McHappyness. Would you like some warmth first, or some space?\" And would you like fries with that?\nPattern 7: Conversational postulates\nA conversational postulate is a sneaky little yes or no question that's actually a way to ask for something indirectly. People use it all the time casually, like, \"Can you pass the salt?\" We already know they're not really asking if you have that ability. In its most egregious form, it could turn into a dare. Do you recall how hard it was as a child to ignore a dare?\nI dare you now to practice this ethical postulate! \"Can my subconscious show me the next healing stepping stone, sparing me any more painful memories than I can handle right now?\"\nPattern 8: Tag questions\nTag questions, like \"isn't it?\" or \"doesn't it?\", can soften a sentence, but they get oily very quickly, so go easy on them."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 9, 5690, 5734, "\n\"Your body knows how to relax, doesn't it?\""], ["Human Written", "High", 27, 5734, 5930, "\nPattern 9: Nominalizations\nA nominalization turns something you do into a noun: you heal, and it becomes 'healing'. Others are 'safety', 'trust', 'integration', 'communion', 'clarity' and 'rest'."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 38, 5930, 6138, " They're a bit vague, and sometimes that's useful, because it lets the listener's subconscious fill in something very specific for them.\n\"A bit more safety can come to me in whatever way my body understands.\""], ["Human Written", "Low", 63, 6138, 6512, "\nPattern 10: Meta Model questions — the de-hypnosis tool\nMilton Model language opens things up, and Meta Model questions ask what exactly someone means. If you want to be ethical with people, you need both.\nWhen something sounds true but vague, ask: \"What do you mean, specifically? According to who? Compared to what? Always, or never? What exactly would happen if you did?"], ["Human Written", "Medium", 53, 6512, 6775, " How do you know that, and what evidence would change your mind?\"\nSo when someone is starting to tense up in their body, use the Milton Model to help them soften. And when you feel you're losing track of what's really going on, that's the time for the Meta Model."]]}
{"name": "r1102-71", "sha256": "0fa316f8167b8daa471ec83a30d5b1a2f4c56c45a43fecfedb014d4d01fb69aa", "words": 241, "headline": "Human Written", "prediction_short": "Human", "fraction_ai": 1.0958254583320518e-23, "fraction_ai_assisted": 0.0, "fraction_human": 1.0, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/d3e104dd-a678-4d3f-9c3c-8e2470603a4a", "utc": "2026-11-02T17:04:46Z", "windows": [["Human Written", "High", 255, 0, 1326, "What I will not use NLP for\nHere is a list of things I don't do with NLP, whether I'm hypnotizing myself or someone else:\nI don't use NLP to convince anyone an intuition is true. For example, I don't use NLP or hypnosis in general, to do more than initial memory retrieval work. Memories retrieved still need external validation, especially when they were led to (which NLP tends to).\nOn the other hand, I also don't use NLP to talk anyone out of a real signal. That doesn't mean we can't try to calm unbearable pain, but we must keep access to the awareness of the signal so that we can do the real root cause healing.\nFor example, I won’t tell anyone to push past their fear before asking what it’s protecting, and I won’t make anyone feel rushed when they want to take time to process the feelings.\nI don't use NLP on people without their consent nor to bypass consent via covert commands. Nearly all hypnotists claim that hypnosis cannot violate consent, which is an absurdly ignorant and unethical claim.\nThat includes not manipulating anyone to feel like their \"no\" is the ego's resistance we need to overcome, which is another way of saying they are spiritually inferior to me if they disagree with me.\nIf someone is in an unstable state in which they can't reasonably give consent, I don't use NLP to pretend they did."]]}
{"name": "r1102-72", "sha256": "3c4ba13cd8ad91bb19d7e826aa7a7ef3507d8f7551da9d79169a1195d0027e9b", "words": 297, "headline": "Human Written", "prediction_short": "Human", "fraction_ai": 7.591979479217134e-26, "fraction_ai_assisted": 1.5571437547426904e-33, "fraction_human": 1.0, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/40f75eef-30e6-493c-ac5c-6ace43b5b82e", "utc": "2026-11-02T17:04:50Z", "windows": [["Human Written", "High", 304, 0, 1698, "Running the whole NLP sequence\nHere is a rough outline of the entire NLP process:\nInduce yourself (meaning gather your attention into a soft focus) or contain yourself (meaning stabilize yourself) first if you are already too opened up to difficult memories/experiences.\nAsk yourself for permission: is it useful to work with this pattern today?\nGet a representation of your pattern. Do you see it as an image, with size, color and location, or do you feel it like a movement or some other kind of sensation?\nFind out if that part/pattern is protecting something for you.\nGently change an aspect of your pattern's representation from the prior step.\nBring in your three good adults. The Nurturer brings love in. Next, the Protector puts your helmet on, and then the Guide points the way out of the mess. They’re really all one inner adult, but picturing each with their own function can be easier before merging them together (like Captain Planet if you saw that cartoon).\nThen anchor the good state you're in with a hand on your heart, two fingers touching, a particular breath or a posture, so that doing the same thing later can bring the state back.\nImagine running into a scenario where your old pattern would have triggered, and adopt a feasible new behavior. (\"If I see a red cloth, then I will choose not to charge at it. I am not a bull anymore.\")\nCheck in with your body for signals during the re-imagining process, and what else besides body signals supports your new interpretation of the situation. Ask yourself whether the new behavior you've imagined is kind and sensible.\nThen come all the way back out of the altered state (see “Come all the way back”), and go do something normal."]]}
{"name": "r1102-73", "sha256": "2c1b33630cfd4f68cb017d31990d47f8622c604fd5e6112f1cf00188e341c10b", "words": 493, "headline": "Human Written", "prediction_short": "Human", "fraction_ai": 1.9061011449772458e-13, "fraction_ai_assisted": 9.707153643200384e-37, "fraction_human": 1.0, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/b00bfdd6-e608-4c52-8574-7ccc0d4191fb", "utc": "2026-11-02T17:04:57Z", "windows": [["Human Written", "High", 43, 0, 271, "Appendix C: The extended de-hypnosis checklist\nWhat to do when you feel like you’re being pushed too hard by something (person, ad, ideology, spiritual teaching, romantic attraction, internal voice, etc.): Say to yourself, “Okay, something is trying to influence me here."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 10, 271, 309, " I don’t have to obey it or attack it."], ["Human Written", "High", 205, 309, 1315, " I can just slow myself down and ask some questions like, 'What would this thing influence me to believe that isn’t true in order to get what it wants from me? What is my body telling me to do about this (how does my body feel)? What would love do here? What would truth do here? How would I approach this humbly? What would life have me do here?'”\nIf what you’re investigating is true, it can take your questioning (as the police like to say). If it’s love, it can accommodate your boundaries. If it’s real guidance, it’ll still be there tomorrow. If it’s really for you, it won’t want you to give up all the wisdom and sovereignty you’ve worked so hard to develop.\nBefore you do what it wants you to do, check how it’s trying to get you there. Is it rushing you, or telling you to keep things secret? Is it shaming you, or threatening to leave you out if you don’t do what it says? Maybe it makes you feel special, or there’s a sexual charge to it, or a sense that you’re spiritually above everyone else."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 27, 1315, 1437, "\nThen look at what it wants from you. Is it money, or sex, or your loyalty? Is it asking you to keep quiet, or to obey it?"], ["Human Written", "High", 233, 1437, 2612, "\nKeep in mind though, people who mean well can ask for some of these too. A teacher charges for their time, and your partner probably wants your loyalty. If you can say no to them and they’re fine with it, that’s a good sign.\nBack to the interrogation:\nIs it trying to narrow down your choices? Does questioning it feel like you’re doing something wrong, or does it act like not obeying is a problem you need to fix? Does normal life start to seem boring, stupid or irrelevant when it’s around? Is it trying to seduce, scare or rescue your inner child? And does it try to stop your adult self from saying no?\nIf it does a bunch of these things, slow yourself down, don’t let it push you deeper into trance, don’t do anything you can’t undo, and then ground yourself for a while (take care of your body, eat, sleep, give it time, get counsel, etc).\nA good guide will make your adult self stronger. A good guide can take no. A bad guide can’t take no. A bad guide wants to take your adult self’s job. A bad guide will try to make your no something that’s bad or needs to be fixed (resistance, ego, fear, low vibration, trauma response, sin, need for more of its guidance, etc)."]]}
{"name": "r1102-74", "sha256": "5112acd88f988a39e4c5b4180fe97ce1d5015276906a643e71e9f1faacae8d86", "words": 275, "headline": "Human Written", "prediction_short": "Human", "fraction_ai": 4.039852173524461e-16, "fraction_ai_assisted": 5.297931387490503e-28, "fraction_human": 1.0, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/ba50558b-2d2e-4270-822f-b51f2547aa1c", "utc": "2026-11-02T17:05:04Z", "windows": [["Human Written", "High", 168, 0, 956, "Hypnosis-specific audit\nBefore you let a hypnotic recording or a live hypnotist put manipulative suggestions into your skull, interview them a bit:\nFirst, what are they going to do to bring you under? And if you react negatively to something, will they pause to change the script? Make sure they are fine with stopping the whole thing.\nAnd how are they deciding it's working? Just because you seem \"out of it\" shouldn't be a green light. Are they using sneaky moves to get past your adult judgement, like putting you into identity roles (including age regression)? Walking you down obedience ladders? Your desire for belonging also shouldn't be used for that.\nKeep in mind though, you can only answer those last questions by reading the script first. You can't expect them to know what your adult judgement would accept, so make that clear ahead of time.\nWill they tell you before they use techniques that affect your memory or behaviors after the session?"], ["Human Written", "Medium", 4, 956, 984, " Like fractionation or cues."], ["Human Written", "High", 113, 984, 1562, "\nAre they low-key using your body signals to prove their theories? Like oh your hand dropped real fast, so you ARE gay.\nAnd when it's time to come out, will they tell you clearly that the session is over, so you get your normal waking, walking self back? After it's over, check how well your critical thinking is working when you look back on how it went.\nIf any answer they give you is wishy washy, beware. Ask for the exact script (or the methods used since they probably aren't exactly reading a script). If they don't want to give the secrets away, walk right out that door."]]}
{"name": "r1102-84", "sha256": "5033a09f3a25a04be3ece7a72b780548ab4f0bd37e701aa2c144a76c38ceeae2", "words": 247, "headline": "Human Written", "prediction_short": "Human", "fraction_ai": 7.016652190209663e-17, "fraction_ai_assisted": 9.865894526901133e-36, "fraction_human": 1.0, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/357637ba-0725-44f5-b7b0-f0f1e72f4e80", "utc": "2026-11-02T17:05:11Z", "windows": [["Human Written", "High", 191, 0, 1018, "Forgiveness without bypass\nWe cannot force forgiveness on ourselves. It has to come from a place of understanding, otherwise it can be bypassing. However, if we remain in the anger forever, we are allowing the injury to dictate how we live our lives in the present. So how do we hold all of this? We just remember that it can all be true at once. They really did hurt us and they still have to answer for it. Our boundary with them is crucial to maintain, especially after forgiveness which can tend to weaken it. One day we may find that we have forgiven them for not knowing better, just like Jesus did on the Cross.\nYou might say to the part of you that got hurt, “I’m not going to use spiritual mumbo jumbo to shush your cries and make you forgive before you're ready. But I’m also not going to build our whole life around this wound forever.”\nForgiving yourself\nFor self-forgiveness, name what you regret doing, and take responsibility for just that part. Let yourself feel the remorse by taking in the harm done."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 7, 1018, 1055, " See how it went against your values."], ["Human Written", "High", 55, 1055, 1348, " Stop short of making yourself a permanent criminal by identifying with the behaviors you're now abandoning.\nDo what you can to put it right. Every so often, come back to how you got to be someone who could do that, until you understand the pattern well enough that it can't drive you anymore."]]}
{"name": "r1102-85", "sha256": "9b94e77da558a369ed6c271c6d5a9887dadd8f4506438bb4c1f54b22e336ac0a", "words": 433, "headline": "Human Written", "prediction_short": "Human", "fraction_ai": 4.5253211663093826e-17, "fraction_ai_assisted": 2.2420775429197073e-44, "fraction_human": 1.0, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/f3716335-310f-43f4-aaa4-dc2ece0644e3", "utc": "2026-11-02T17:05:16Z", "windows": [["Human Written", "High", 263, 0, 1341, "Appendix G: Altered states\nI’m not saying you should use substances, but many people have used them when they first did self-hypnosis, contacted their inner child, or talked to their Higher Self. I’d learn the inner child work sober first, with enough Nurturer and Protector in the room before you go deep (see the inner child reparenting section). If you don’t have them in you yet, borrow them from someone steady, as long as they won’t take advantage of that to try to run your trip for you.\nDo not use altered states to try to force yourself to get to a certain revelation about yourself, but rather to help yourself become more in tune with love and to better your life.\nA lot of people have had dramatic openings to love at some point in their life. If you've had a similar experience, you know that there is a difference between having experienced it at one point, or only being able to access it in a certain state, and being able to get to it at any point in your life. While you're building a way to reach love on a normal day, let that experience you had serve as a reference point for what can happen. (If you can't give that love to the child, try to deal with why you can't, instead of trying to ramp up the experience. Often there's a child guard part that’s seen love come with strings or get revoked before in a painful way."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 10, 1341, 1399, " Love starts with hearing out the resistance to it first.)"], ["Human Written", "High", 179, 1399, 2398, "\nUse your altered state of consciousness, either while you're in it or after, to help yourself by asking things like:\nHelp me to become more grounded. Help me to only take what I can integrate. Help me to remember love. Help me to come back when it's time. Help me to figure out how to change one thing in my life to make it better.\nDon’t use self-hypnosis to try to keep the altered state of consciousness going indefinitely, to force memories to come back, to make yourself more afraid, to get by without sleep, to put off taking care of medical problems, to become less communicative, etc.\nIn other words, if using self-hypnosis while you're in an altered state of consciousness isn't helping you become more loving, more grounded, more honest with yourself, sleep better, become more communicative and more able to do your everyday responsibilities, etc, then stop trying to go deeper into your altered state of consciousness, and start working on integrating what you've already gotten from it."]]}
{"name": "r1102-99", "sha256": "96cd6a8b3c0f6c57b86f24ee716b596978b1f56636f577bd639983ae593bb880", "words": 323, "headline": "Human Written", "prediction_short": "Human", "fraction_ai": 1.83324275898622e-12, "fraction_ai_assisted": 1.0362723292644615e-18, "fraction_human": 1.0, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/980437b6-2192-4223-afef-d79c3b68486b", "utc": "2026-11-02T17:05:23Z", "windows": [["Human Written", "Medium", 1, 0, 2, "8."], ["Human Written", "High", 48, 2, 273, " Resource embodiment\nPick a quality you understand and want more of, like warmth, being able to hold a boundary, steadiness, curiosity or dignity. Imagine yourself with just 1% more of it. (If you'd rather not step into it, you can watch an imagined you have it instead.)"], ["Human Written", "Medium", 3, 273, 291, " What's different?"], ["Human Written", "High", 49, 291, 538, " How do you sit, and how does your voice sound? Try it a few times; each time, it gets a little easier to find. Come back, keeping the quality and a positive action that you would do with it, but leaving the imagined you behind, saying \"I am me\".\n"], ["Human Written", "Medium", 1, 538, 540, "9."], ["Human Written", "High", 235, 540, 1819, " No-trance inner contact\nWe don't need to go into trance to get a lot of the benefits of the communion technique! Here's my no-trance version:\nFor pacing (warm-up), notice reality as it is now. What do you see around you? Is today Monday, your favorite day of the week? Hopefully your name didn't suddenly change to Larry.\nFor the suggestion: in your mind, ask a clear question and then listen gently.\nNow keep your sense of agency during the answer phase. You might notice an answer popped up, or you might decide you don't know. You can always take a break or rephrase the question. Sometimes you might ask advice from someone else.\nKeep aware of the subtle inner signal: write whatever you get. It might be a word or sensation. An impulse or objection. Sometimes there's no signal, just silence, itself a kind of signal. Don't jump to interpreting it as validation of some theory.\nHand off the role: have your adult self answer that same question in whatever way is appropriate, preferably by writing or doing.\nIntegration/exit: reality test the signal you noticed. As part of testing, if it seems appropriate, you can do something simple based on it.\nThere's no elaborate exit protocol here since you didn't go into trance. Just close the exercise and carry on with your day."]]}
{"name": "r1102-E-107", "sha256": "3d70992148c7000064c2b8512f0cf5e13e12020b9886fa2c25679d97fbffb564", "words": 207, "headline": "Human Written", "prediction_short": "Human", "fraction_ai": 6.891770415372784e-36, "fraction_ai_assisted": 0.0, "fraction_human": 1.0, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/f190c7af-a869-47a8-9508-40b92de1adf8", "utc": "2026-11-02T17:05:27Z", "windows": [["Human Written", "High", 211, 0, 1112, "Let the child speak while you define the goal\nYour inner child wants to be heard, but they don't want to feel like they have to steer the ship while they're in the emotional storm. By providing this protective healing guidance for them, you gain access to all of the positive aspects of what it can be like to be as free as an unburdened child. All the wonder, silliness, approaching things through the senses more, feeling it’s ok to be vulnerable, to want someone to take care of you, to feel need without the stigma of \"needy,\" and to want to offload some decision making, while your adult part stays present. At the same time you get to leave behind the difficulties that came with really being a kid: having to obey, not being able to do much for yourself, getting scolded, and not understanding how things work yet.\n\"It is okay for a younger part of me to talk. I understand that the adult in me is always going to be here, listening, evaluating, protecting me and stopping me if needed. I'm not handing my adult decisions over to a younger part of me, or to a hypnotist or a recording, or to anyone else.\""]]}
{"name": "r1102-E-315", "sha256": "2743950a682646a02fd04b947c0e55d548e66579babe66162c48d62c0ee04d34", "words": 170, "headline": "Human Written", "prediction_short": "Human", "fraction_ai": 1.9077220170641672e-22, "fraction_ai_assisted": 1.3563095313346986e-29, "fraction_human": 1.0, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/186da340-7c81-4ba1-a095-a10a97856c6b", "utc": "2026-11-02T17:05:31Z", "windows": [["Human Written", "High", 178, 0, 968, "If your recording happens to cut out partway through, woops... you could end up lying there dazed & confused, waiting on a voice that isn't coming back. Don't worry, you don't have to be a vegetable forever. Just tell yourself, \"The recording has stopped and we're all done now. Welcome back to me!\" (that exclamation actually helps, because trance is kinda monotone). Then do the exit-trance count and the present-time checks above on your own. Once your eyes are open, \"touch grass\" as they say, for grounding. Or if no grass, just push your adorable feet or hands into something solid. The physical feeling connects your brain to your body.\nSleep recordings are another story, since you're assuming you'll drift off midway with those. But if the sleep recording is designed to also wake you back up, make sure it's doing so intelligently, not just using a vague exit word that might half wake you up and still leave you a bit blank or \"under the spell\" so to speak."]]}
{"name": "r1102-E-368", "sha256": "638652059270b308eb04ac0edc1c11e06371f3e3f1f42f5ac67f1c25aa44ab2b", "words": 149, "headline": "Human Written", "prediction_short": "Human", "fraction_ai": 1.1978125739539602e-12, "fraction_ai_assisted": 1.5862040413788803e-14, "fraction_human": 1.0, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/5c2a9a66-8ecc-4e87-8782-2278d51b98b7", "utc": "2026-11-02T17:05:35Z", "windows": [["Human Written", "High", 84, 0, 452, "Once or twice a week, when it’s useful, give this practice more space and time so even the unplanned, unknown and maybe hidden needs can show up. Just because it's unplanned doesn't mean it will be more shocking. Start from your Higher Self, from the field of acceptance and understanding, or however you can describe it that makes it feel accessible. If you need the Protector or another of your adult jobs, bring it in or borrow it from someone safe."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 3, 452, 463, " Mr. or Ms."], ["Human Written", "High", 67, 463, 816, " Protector can check to make sure you’re not skipping past anything important. Leave enough time at the end to come all the way back up & out.\nThen, if there's something from the session that asked you to do something in real life, and your Protector agrees, then go ahead and do it when you can. That's how you show your subconscious you mean business."]]}
{"name": "r1102-E-406", "sha256": "a1565c631a5ce1e1aac8c872a1b415213960ba3611bdb6c997075ea96acefbbb", "words": 71, "headline": "Human Written", "prediction_short": "Human", "fraction_ai": 3.955508816149526e-25, "fraction_ai_assisted": 3.8499274008860024e-41, "fraction_human": 1.0, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/65b23a2a-d0a8-46c6-8fee-ad73d6e41741", "utc": "2026-11-02T17:05:40Z", "windows": [["Human Written", "High", 74, 0, 366, "You become too blissful or diffuse\nIf the bliss spreads out into a big warm haze, it can’t do much for you or anyone else yet. Bring it down to Earth by asking, “What’s this lofty love asking me to do? Is there a task I'm ignoring? Or a boundary I need to set? Am I getting enough rest and nourishment? Am I hiding from a needed conversation or relationship repair?”"]]}
